Falsifies `system_tests::user::std_threads_tests::rayons_parallel_sum_runs_on_every_online_core`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect, in milestone 812 (`std::thread::spawn` runs real threads in one address space): a
member that its process's end finished where it was blocked is never reaped, because nothing
switches it out again. `rayon`'s idle workers are asleep on a futex when `main` returns, so the
process keeps its workers' corpses and its space until its region is destroyed. The four-thread test
joins every thread before it exits and cannot see this.

Expected to fail: "std_rayon's process did not end with all its threads reaped".

Regenerated 2026-10-11 (UTC) for milestone 840 (the scheduler file is split along its seams):
the same lines, moved out of `kernel/src/sched.rs` into `kernel/src/sched.rs` unchanged, so the defect is
the same and only the path and line numbers differ.

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched/switch.rs b/kernel/src/sched/switch.rs
index 82ba2d245..027fe8963 100644
--- a/kernel/src/sched/switch.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/sched/switch.rs
@@ -579,7 +579,5 @@ pub(super) fn reap_switched_out(
         .and_then(|s| s.threads.get(prev))
         .and_then(|t| t.process);
     process::reap_corpse(guard, prev);
-    if let Some(pid) = process {
-        process::reap_corpses(pid); // members its end finished where they were blocked
-    }
